<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46801" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sŭper-lĭno</span></b> , no <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>perf.</i>,
				lĭtum, 3, v. a., <i>to daub</i> or <i>smear over</i>
			(post-Aug.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To daub</i> or <i>smear</i> a thing
				<i>over</i> something: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">radicem in vino decoctam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					27, 6, 24, § 42</span></i>
			. — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To smear over</i>, <i>besmear</i>
			with something: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">laser visco, ut haereat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					22, 23, 49, § 103</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dolium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Pall. Oct. 14, 5</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
